 Heffter's difference problem.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDense halves in balanced 2-partition of K4-free graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.13485)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.9 years ago; Balogh, Clemen, and Lidick\\'y conjectured that for every $K_4$-free graph on $n$ (even) vertices, there exists a balanced 2-partition $A,A^c$ such that $\\max\\{e(A),e(A^c)\\}\\leq n^2/16$ edges. In this paper, we present a family of counterexamples to the conjecture and provide a new upper bound ($0.074n^2$) for every sufficiently large even integer $n$.\nTitle: Dense halves in balanced 2-partition of K4-free graphs\nAuthors: Yue Xu, Xiao-Dong Zhang\nDate: Wed Dec 18 04:00:31 2024\n\nA balanced 2-partition of a graph is a bipartition $A,A^c$ of $V(G)$ such that $|A|=|A^c|$. Balogh, Clemen, and Lidick\\'y conjectured that for every $K_4$-free graph on $n$ (even) vertices, there exists a balanced 2-partition $A,A^c$ such that $\\max\\{e(A),e(A^c)\\}\\leq n^2/16$ edges. In this paper, we present a family of counterexamples to the conjecture and provide a new upper bound ($0.074n^2$) for every sufficiently large even integer $n$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTriangle decompositions of PG(n - 1,2) — Lacuna (https://lacuna.tiptreesystems.com/work/triangle-decompositions-of-pg-n-1-2/wrk_f93f7ec8d3d8da552fe990e6e748ebab)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Krotov ... These designs are crucial for understanding the structure of these spaces and have implications for combinatorial design theory, particularly in the context of subspace designs and graph decompositions. ...   * Balanced Triangle Designs for n ≡ 1 (mod 6): The paper constructs balanced triangle designs in PG(n-1, 2) for all admissible parameters n congruent to 1 modulo 6 (Theorem 7). ...   * Conjecture for n ≡ 0, 1 (mod 6): The authors conjecture that symmetric triangle designs exist for all prime n congruent to 0 or 1 modulo 6, but this remains an open problem.\n\n# Triangle decompositions of PG(n - 1,2)\n\nMinjia Shi, Xiaoxiao Li, Denis S. Krotov\n\nDiscret. Math 2026 · DOI\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThis paper constructs balanced triangle designs in projective spaces over the field with two elements (F₂). These designs are crucial for understanding the structure of these spaces and have implications for combinatorial design theory, particularly in the context of subspace designs and graph decompositions.\n\n## What Problem Does This Paper Address?\n\nThe paper tackles the problem of constructing \"balanced triangle designs\" within projective geometries, specifically PG(n-1, 2). A triangle design is a way to partition all the lines in a projective space into sets of three lines that form \"triangles\" (three pairwise intersecting lines with no common point). A \"balanced\" design means that every point in the projective space is involved in the same number of these triangles. Constructing such balanced designs, especially for specific parameters of the projective space (like its dimension), is a challenging combinatorial problem. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ngraph-conjectures/ARXIV_OPEN_DIFFICULTY_RANKING.md at main · graph-theory-AI/graph-conjectures · GitHub (https://github.com/graph-theory-AI/graph-conjectures/blob/main/ARXIV_OPEN_DIFFICULTY_RANKING.md)\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; 43  | 4.10  | 4  | prove  | open  | `AX_kst_minor_free_choosable_k44_k35` (`2201.09115__00`)  | Question 1  | Disproof of a Conjecture by Woodall  | Both questions remain open as of May 2026. ... 147  | 3.50  | 4  | balanced  | open  | `AX_kst_minor_free_choosable_woodall_fixed_s` (`2201.09115__02`)  | Open problem: Woodall's conjecture for fixed s  | Disproof of a Conjecture by Woodall  | The specific regime of fixed $s$ and $t\\to \\mathrm{\\infty }$ for Woodall's conjecture (that eve